"<strong>Through the year at Ruston.</strong> Press <strong>Pause</strong> (the demo opens playing). Leave the <strong>Observer latitude</strong> slider at {#}° N and <strong>Axial tilt ε</strong> at {#}°, where they open. Set the <strong>Date</strong> slider to the 21st of February, April, June, August, October and December, and press <strong>Record reading</strong> at each ({#} readings). The readout beside the slider shows the date and the day number: these 21sts are days {#}, {#}, {#}, {#}, {#} and {#}. Drag close, then the arrow keys step one day. Then press <strong>Export to worksheet</strong> and <strong>Clear</strong>.",
"<strong>Distance alone.</strong> Press the <strong>No tilt</strong> setup; it sets Axial tilt ε to {#}° and keeps {#}° N. Set the <strong>Date</strong> slider to the 21st of January, March, May, July, September and November (days {#}, {#}, {#}, {#}, {#} and {#}), press <strong>Record reading</strong> at each ({#} readings), then press <strong>Export to worksheet</strong> and <strong>Clear</strong>.",
